# Libretro (README.md): plays games for classic consoles on the built-in
# screen, or a TV on the HDMI port, with libretro emulator cores (the same
# cores RetroArch uses). Up to four players with gamepads.
NAME="Libretro"
SUMMARY="Play NES, Game Boy and GBA games with libretro cores, on a TV too, two players with gamepads (more consoles with downloadable cores)"
APP_VERSION="1.4.0"
# Debian's libretro cores for NES (Nestopia), Game Boy / Color (Gambatte) and
# Game Boy Advance (mGBA); curl and unzip to download more cores (SNES, Mega
# Drive, PC Engine, PlayStation...) into ~/Games/cores from libretro's nightly
# builds, from the Libretro app. The sound goes through aplay, from alsa-utils in
# the base image (not listed: it brings kmod, which apt would leave behind).
DEPENDS="libretro-nestopia, libretro-gambatte, libretro-mgba, curl, unzip"
